{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave","id":1443157,"title":"Gotham City by Night a.k.a \"To the Bat Cave!\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-08T13:02:20-07:00","id":1443157,"title":"Gotham City by Night a.k.a \"To the Bat Cave!\"","content":"I freely admit to currently running Gotham City by Night where Batman was the Old Clan Tzimisce Prince and opposed by the Malkavian Antitribu Joker.<br /> <br /> The PCs' territory is Bludhaven, which I'm basically doing as Gary meets Detroit exaggerated to comic book levels.<br /> <br /> I'm having a lot of fun with the sheer silliness of playing &quot;The DC Universe except everyone is a vampire&quot; weirdness.<br /> <br /> Vandal Savage is the head of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any ideas how they'd adapt things from the DCU (or Hell, Marvel) to V:TM?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T13:05:03-07:00","id":1443158,"title":"","content":"Expected Response:<br /> <br /> &quot;Why make Batman into a Tzimisce? Wouldn't Ventrue be more appropriate? Hell, even a Gangrel?&quot;<br /> <br /> Answer: Because I wanted to.<br /> <br /> Mind you, making Kirk Langstrom into a Tzimisce would have probably worked better as contrast. I made him a Camazotz instead.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T13:42:57-07:00","id":1443164,"title":"","content":"Is it more like the comics or the movies?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T13:44:07-07:00","id":1443165,"title":"","content":"Or the cartoons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T13:49:46-07:00","id":1443166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443164#post1443164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it more like the comics or the movies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's still a Vampire: The Masquerade chronicle so I go full Tim Burton and R-Rated for the universe. I probably draw from the characters in the cartoons just because that's in my mind but my Gotham City is a bunch of huge spiraling buildings, gargoyles, and excessive poverty at the bottom. I suppose that oddly makes it most like the video game, ARKHAM ASYLUM, series that is the &quot;R-rated version of the television show&quot; in terms of themes and appearance.<br /> <br /> Obviously everyone is a lot meaner when they're now possessed of the Beasts.<br /> <br /> Weirdly, I do actually give my Bat-Prince a killing aversion. Whenever possible, he ends up staking and imprisoning vampires than destroying them. Its later speculated that Arkham Asylum has an ancient vampire underneath it that he is feeding to keep asleep.<br /> <br /> (True: But it's not blood. It's nightmares and the Ancient underneath Arkham is Malakai, Malkav's sister)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T17:10:57-07:00","id":1443191,"title":"","content":"This would make for a great no mans land story with all the coteries matching up with one of the gangs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T17:16:55-07:00","id":1443194,"title":"","content":"<b>Poison Ivy </b>is the last Lhiannan!<br /> <br /> Or maybe not last since Jason Woodrue presumably still exists.<br /> <br /> <b>Harley</b> is a Sabbat defector to the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <b>Penguin</b> strikes me as someone that I would make a Gangrel who is severely irritated that he's not a Ventrue. Another option is that he is a Nosferatu that is just SLIGHTLY deformed but still off-putting enough to repulse everyone. Both have the disciplines that would fit his heavy Animalism use.<br /> <br /> <b>Two-Face </b>being a Malkavian is pretty obvious as well. So is the <b>Riddler</b>, <b>Scarecrow</b>, and other lunatics at Arkham Asylum.<br /> <br /> <b>Killer Croc: </b>Nosferatu. Duh.<br /> <br /> <b>Clayface: </b>Maybe a Nosferatu with Vicissitude? It reverts every night?<br /> <br /> <b>Thomas Elliot </b>a.k.a Hush being a Tzimisce makes sense with his shapeshifting/plastic surgeon powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Ra's Al Ghul</b> I would make to be a 6th-7th generation Banu Haqim or Follower of Set at the head of his own Blood Cult or part of the Black Hand. I'm leaning to Banu Haqim because they have some honor.<br /> <br /> <b>Catwoman</b> I will probably make as an Embraced Bastet Kinfolk because no way she'd hang around Bruce if she wasn't a vampire but Gangrel isn't quite enough for her animal fetishism. I don't buy any sort of Underworld-esque romance in the WOD either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-08-2021, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T18:11:57-07:00","id":1443197,"title":"","content":"I have always been of the mind that Batman would be a Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> Poison Ivy as a Bahari comes to mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T18:30:16-07:00","id":1443198,"title":"","content":"<b>Gotham City by Night</b><br /> <br /> Bruce Wayne, Prince of Gotham City since the 1930s, has entered torpor after having his back broken by the mysterious Brujah warlord known as Bane. The city has suffered numerous crises like Earthquakes and civil unrest. Bruce's eldest childe, Dick Grayson, has proven unequal or uninterested in the task of assuming the Princedom. Rumors spread he prefers to work as an Archon for the Camarilla with a group of mixed supernatural mercenaries known as the Titans.<br /> <br /> As a result, Gotham City is torn by civil war between the various factions ranging from Toreador Vesper Lynd to the authoritarian Deathstroke. The only bright spot in the city is that Joker, leader of the Sabbat's ongoing crusade against the Prince, has also disappeared. Some attributing it to the Kindred assassin known as the Red Hood who has sent a dozen vampires to their Final Death.<br /> <br /> As one of the richest and most sought-after domains in the world, Gotham City is ripe for the taking, At present, no one controls enough territory or has enough favors to be Prince but even Neonates could theoretically take a smaller city-sized chunk out of the brooding city for themselves. Bruce Wayne was an unconventional prince, more prone to mercy and dark justice than many, but his legacy has been inconsistent. Do you seek to uphold it or supplant it? What happens when (if?) he returns?<br /> <br /> <b>Mood</b><br /> <br /> The Gothic Punk elements of the World of Darkness are dialed up to the eleven. The skyscrapers have gargoyles, loom over the poor, and the entire place has a kind of Neo Dark Ages feel. Everything is starkly contrasted with inbred insane Old Money families in crumbling mansions, a hideously corrupt police force, vast numbers of criminals propping up a dysfunctional economy, and the poor living in fear. It is a city divorced from time and the real world but all the more terrifying for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme</b><br /> <br /> Can vampires ever be the lesser evil? Gotham City is a pit and if the werewolves were to ever restart the Impergium, it would not be the worst place to begin. However, it's previous Prince tried to use his money and influence to fix it. It is a place with no end of evil doers, human or otherwise, that compete with the PCs as predators. The PCs could try to thin the ranks of the evils around them or perhaps genuinely make things better. Even a pragmatic villain who merely wants their prey to be docile is better than the chaos of a city of madmen.<br /> <br /> But are all things they touch doomed by the Curse of Caine?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T20:11:05-07:00","id":1443206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443194#post1443194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Poison Ivy </b>is the last Lhiannan!<br /> <br /> Or maybe not last since Jason Woodrue presumably still exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>IF we are going full WOD I'd say Ivy, Woodrue, swamp thing are Kami. But that comes off as abit boring. Honestly all Three start as SCIENCE villains who cross into mysticism. I think you might get something interesting with Ivy as a Etherite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Harley</b> is a Sabbat defector to the Anarchs. </div> </div> </div>Harley is a Ghoul, or at least that's her story with Joker. Depending where you want to put her story at some point she breaks away but her time with the Joker is the abusiveness that is a ghoul. Honestly I think maybe her going some flavour of Hunter might be the right way out of her story. Of course if she's teaming up with Ivy... a pair of Etherites could be an interesting look there. Harley could pull off being an Adventurer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Penguin</b> strikes me as someone that I would make a Gangrel who is severely irritated that he's not a Ventrue. Another option is that he is a Nosferatu that is just SLIGHTLY deformed but still off-putting enough to repulse everyone. Both have the disciplines that would fit his heavy Animalism use. </div> </div> </div>Penguin has never been really an animalism type. But he has been a nice fat caniabal from a twisted various twisted old bloodlines. I would say... he might make a good Embraced Revanant or make the cobblepots a Giovanni family. Dominate and Potence works really good for various interpretations of him. That he doesn't &quot;Do the Necromancy thing&quot; is something the fluff pushes if not the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Two-Face </b>being a Malkavian is pretty obvious as well. So is the <b>Riddler</b>, <b>Scarecrow</b>, and other lunatics at Arkham Asylum. </div> </div> </div>I think things get a little too one Note if everyone is Malkavian. Two-Face should be, but being Nos also might work. Scarecrow is like Mr Freize or Hugo Strange they are a different sort of messed up. Hugo Strange and Scarecrow are messed in in a &quot;I'm on a Path&quot; messed up and not a derangement messed up so I'd make make them tzim. Though scarecrow could really be any clan known for its intellectual detachement, Trujah, Tremere. Fear is a science for him.<br /> <br /> I would make the Ventriloquist a Malkavian... but he's also a medium. Scarface is Real. His derangement is something else.<br /> <br /> Just to mix it up I'd make The Riddler some sort of changeling. His methology feels very fae. That or a Kiyasid or Maeghar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Clayface: </b>Maybe a Nosferatu with Vicissitude? It reverts every night? </div> </div> </div>He's A tzim experiment. Or he's working on some sort of Vic technique and... hasn't quite worked out the kinks yet. Honestly making him one of those freak experimental embraces that creates a new bloodline seems a simple choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ra's Al Ghul</b> I would make to be a 6th-7th generation Banu Haqim or Follower of Set at the head of his own Blood Cult or part of the Black Hand. I'm leaning to Banu Haqim because they have some honor. </div> </div> </div>Make him the Eldest of the Schism? If you wanted a different take.. making him Bruce's Sire or grandsire would give some fun options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Catwoman</b> I will probably make as an Embraced Bastet Kinfolk because no way she'd hang around Bruce if she wasn't a vampire but Gangrel isn't quite enough for her animal fetishism. I don't buy any sort of Underworld-esque romance in the WOD either. </div> </div> </div>catwoman is perhaps the most variant.but she's generally not a &quot;big cat&quot; vibe. Honestly she feels more like a Toreador with her need to steal pretty things with a very specialized take on what she wants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T20:16:59-07:00","id":1443207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443206#post1443206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IF we are going full WOD I'd say Ivy, Woodrue, swamp thing are Kami. But that comes off as abit boring. Honestly all Three start as SCIENCE villains who cross into mysticism. I think you might get something interesting with Ivy as a Etherite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think that Ivy would be a vampire because she's very much a seductive and mind-controlling plant master as well as a scientist and nature abomination. But that's just me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Harley is a Ghoul, or at least that's her story with Joker. Depending where you want to put her story at some point she breaks away but her time with the Joker is the abusiveness that is a ghoul. Honestly I think maybe her going some flavour of Hunter might be the right way out of her story. Of course if she's teaming up with Ivy... a pair of Etherites could be an interesting look there. Harley could pull off being an Adventurer. </div> </div> </div>Harley being under the Blood Bond and breaking it seems to me more Kindred. She's certainly not a henchman and disposable mook at some point since she's able to stand up to Batman and Joker as her own antiheroine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Penguin has never been really an animalism type. But he has been a nice fat caniabal from a twisted various twisted old bloodlines. I would say... he might make a good Embraced Revanant or make the cobblepots a Giovanni family. Dominate and Potence works really good for various interpretations of him. That he doesn't &quot;Do the Necromancy thing&quot; is something the fluff pushes if not the mechanics. </div> </div> </div>The Penguin does have armies of birds, his pet shark, and various other animal minions, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think things get a little too one Note if everyone is Malkavian. Two-Face should be, but being Nos also might work. Scarecrow is like Mr Freize or Hugo Strange they are a different sort of messed up. Hugo Strange and Scarecrow are messed in in a &quot;I'm on a Path&quot; messed up and not a derangement messed up so I'd make make them tzim. Though scarecrow could really be any clan known for its intellectual detachement, Trujah, Tremere. Fear is a science for him. </div> </div> </div>I'd say Strange would work best as a Tremere. There's a very obsessive work ethic and genius that fits him.<br /> <br /> Scarecrow could also be Tremere with just a focus on a very specific sort of research.<br /> <br /> Mr. Freeze is definitely someone who kind of needs to be something other than a vampire, you're right. Maybe you could do Tremere or his own unique bloodline but that loses just about everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would make the Ventriloquist a Malkavian... but he's also a medium. Scarface is Real. His derangement is something else. </div> </div> </div>That's a very good idea.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I also worry that the more esoteric you go with vampire, the more you potentially lose the coolness of the simple, &quot;He's a vampire and that by itself is pretty crazy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-08-2021, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T20:55:19-07:00","id":1443211,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=CTPhipps;n1443207]<br /> <br /> Eh, I think that Ivy would be a vampire because she's very much a seductive and mind-controlling plant master as well as a scientist and nature abomination. But that's just me.{/quote]<br /> <br /> Except when she's not there alot of interpretations of her. But making her some toreador bloodline with a connection to plants would work. Presence, Auspex Green Path? Nothing really sounds Pagan blood goddess about her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Harley being under the Blood Bond and breaking it seems to me more Kindred. She's certainly not a henchman and disposable mook at some point since she's able to stand up to Batman and Joker as her own antiheroine. </div> </div> </div>I feel the power dynamics even of generation just aren't there if she's fully embraced with the Joker. Her story when she was with the Joker was using her as a distraction at best for Batman. She definately gains levels in comptience with her full on protagnist status though<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Penguin does have armies of birds, his pet shark, and various other animal minions, though. </div> </div> </div>I've never considered it a core concept of the character but I am sure he's had all sorts of pets over the years. Him being the &quot;neutral&quot; figure anyone can talk to. HIm being Neutral ground.. feels Giovanni really.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say Strange would work best as a Tremere. There's a very obsessive work ethic and genius that fits him.<br /> <br /> Scarecrow could also be Tremere with just a focus on a very specific sort of research. </div> </div> </div>They would be very much Ordo in a different World of Darkness...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mr. Freeze is definitely someone who kind of needs to be something other than a vampire, you're right. Maybe you could do Tremere or his own unique bloodline but that loses just about everything. </div> </div> </div>Mr Freeze like Solmon Grundy is.. an out of context problem that shows up to remind them vampires aren't the only thing. I don't think they are regular players just... when they show up in the city its a problem for everyone. They don't care about the Masquerade or the rule of shade or whatever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a very good idea.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I also worry that the more esoteric you go with vampire, the more you potentially lose the coolness of the simple, &quot;He's a vampire and that by itself is pretty crazy.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You're doing batman villains as Vampires its... going to have issues and I've always liked the idea that scarface is more than JUST his crazy. But I am also a big fan of &quot;the world pf darkness is filled with wierd shit that falls outside the easy answers&quot;<br /> <br /> Having the players spend time unraveling the mystery of what the scarface is, is plot by itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T23:34:45-07:00","id":1443214,"title":"","content":"I imagine a city Dominated by Malkavians, playing a play they've been playing for near a hundred years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T23:43:21-07:00","id":1443215,"title":"","content":"This is so ridiculously dumb that I love it. Here are some suggestions. I am using any media depiction as an inspiration so expect various Adam West TV references as well as some odd characters from the comics.<br /> <br /> King Tut as a Follower of Set. He leads the local temple.<br /> <br /> I have always loved Roddy McDowell as the Boomworm on the Adam West TV Show. He was almost as malevolent as Frank Gorshin's Riddler. He could make another Malkavian or perhaps a Toreador with a love of books and fine editions. The Bookworm is probably the best of the celebrity villains created specifically for the show. I find Roddy in general to be awesome.<br /> <br /> Nocturna and Night-Thief/Night-Slayer have to be in there as well. These are Pre-Crisis characters from the early 1980s. Both are very gothic characters, and Nocturna had many qualities of a vampire. I'd probably make them Toreador, but implied incestuous desires between these two siblings and Nocturna's corpselike appearance might suggest them as Giovanni.<br /> <br /> You need the Monk and Dala! Both were actual vampires in the Batman comics, and even turned Batman and Robin temporarily into a vampire in the early 1980s. They date back to the Golden Age! The obvious thing for you to do is make the Monk into Batman's sire and Dala as his broodmate.<br /> <br /> Julie Madison (Bruce's original fiance in the Golden Age) needs to be included as a ghoul! I think most of his civilian love interests work best as a ghoul harem. But not all!<br /> <br /> Silver St Cloud as a Lupine. Silver Fang of course. Maybe she was a possible love interest before Bruce was changed. (Wonder Woman the rest of the Amazons would of course be Black Furies.)<br /> <br /> Vickie Vale as a reporter wanting to uncover the existence of vampires in Gotham. Another human antagonist.<br /> <br /> Firefly as a vampire hunter. Keep him human as no vampire would wield fire like that. If you have to make him a vampire, make him Tremere with an obsession with Lure of Flames.<br /> <br /> Deadshot would make a good vampire hunter too.<br /> <br /> Jim Gordon as another vampire hunter because Batman embraced Barbara Gordon!<br /> <br /> Thomas and Martha Wayne as wraiths who haunt their son. Batman should have the Haunted flaw. He's one of their fetters.<br /> <br /> And you need Ace the bathound as his ghouled dog!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T04:01:07-07:00","id":1443236,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's been deeply fun and deeply stupid too.<br /> <br /> All very good suggestions!<br /> <br /> Some ideas I am now having:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mr. Freeze</b> as a outside context problem would work very well if you wanted to make him into a Son of Ether with lots of Paradox that he's dealing with. Maybe even verging on Marauder-dom and just stepping out of sci-fi Pulp in the vampire's world. Maybe his delusion is his wife is still alive and not DEAD inside his crogenics chamber (mind you, that's not an issue for mages necessarily). It actually explains why Batman and company can survive their fights with Freeze because they can survive being frozen better than most poor bastards.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Solomon Grundy</b> as a Revenant or Frankenstein's monster or full-on Abomination is a pretty good character. If you're ever going to use a monster that is overpowered, impressive rage, and a creature that should not exist then this is the best one to do. You might even make it clear that poor Batman doesn't even know what he is.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Jim Gordon</b> could be Batman's ghoul and contact for the police for most of his career but their relationship destroyed by his Embrace of her. Perhaps after she gets shot by the Joker. It would be a nicely dark way of turning things with him being a independent ghoul who needs regular blood to survive and working with the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> 4. The entire Bat-Family works as a kind of brood of the Prince with most of them being his clan but you could have <b>Cassandra Cain</b> as an adopted Banu Haqim character and <b>Spoiler</b> as something like a 13th generation Caitiff or Malkavian that Bruce is kind of dismissive. Hell, make her a Thin Blood and increase the tragedy/humanity of the character.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>King Tut</b> as the world's worst Follower of Set, like Marcel on steroids, amuses me to no end. You could actually do the same with <b>Maxie Zeus</b> who is kind of the same character too as there's no problem with Hellene Ministry characters too. After all, is it pretending to be a god if you are?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T05:30:16-07:00","id":1443248,"title":"","content":"A big question is how much of a &quot;Masquerade&quot; do you want for this? (Or other-splat equivalent). Batman is relatively low-key compared to even the milder forms of Superman. <br /> <br /> Given &quot;world of darkness&quot; I like the Idea of a Malkavian Batman that drives people mad and turns them into his comic-book enemies; the overwhelming majority of Batman Villains are, after all, mad, kinda like how most of spider-man's enemies are either scientists or engineers or own a company focusing on science and engineering. <br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps not malks: <br /> Penguin should be a Ventrue, perhaps a Toreador (or malkavian... or a ravnos?) . The whole deformity thing doesn't work as well as a rich man in a dapper suit doing crimes for fun. <br /> Poison Ivy just happens to know the green path. Perhaps she's an Assamite too. <br /> Bane is a very erudite Brujah. <br /> Dr Freeze is kinda the most difficult one because everyone fits so well into vampire* that I don't want to bring in a mage. We could have him a Caitiff inceptor, a rogue Tremere with an Ice-based path, a Koldun... there are options, certainly. <br /> <br /> *Wraith, Formor and demons are close enough to vampire that it's not much of a tonal shift to use them. <br /> <br /> I'd be gentle and 'Batman' would really have a lot of 4's and 3's as stats, none of that 'peak human in everything' crap (well, he could do that with drugs and tech, I wouldn't be adverse to that) <br /> <br /> Animalism 3, Ausp 3, Celerity 2, Dementation 5, Fortitude 3, Flight 2 (needing a gliding cape) Obf 5, Obtenebration 2, Potence 3, Protean 2, Thaumaturgy 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T06:21:58-07:00","id":1443250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443248#post1443248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big question is how much of a &quot;Masquerade&quot; do you want for this? (Or other-splat equivalent). Batman is relatively low-key compared to even the milder forms of Superman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine that a World of Darkness Gotham City is a place where the supernatural is still covered up but the Masquerade would be holding only barely. This would be the &quot;Batman is an urban legend&quot; sort of story where he's well known among the supernaturals (albeit you might have it a secret that the Prince's &quot;Enforcer&quot; is the same man as the Prince himself). The people of Gotham City know there's a shit ton of unsolved murders, weird killers, and unexplainable phenomenon in their town but the police always deny it. However, the Masquerade is paper in Crime Alley or other Wasteland-esque areas. They may not believe in VAMPIRES per se but they certainly believe in stories of Candyman-esque Jokers and guys living in the sewers who eat people.<br /> <br /> Which is an interesting needle to thread.<br /> <br /> Hell, maybe they know the &quot;broken police light&quot; they never replace is a secret signal to the sky for the Prince.<br /> <br /> As for Superman, I'd be tempted to replace Mithras with him.<br /> <br /> An ancient powerful vampire god that is the &quot;heroic&quot; ruler of Metropolis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T10:14:36-07:00","id":1443273,"title":"","content":"What about all of the bat family! <br /> <br /> Including Cassandra Cain. I guess she\u2019s a assimite trained since birth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T11:19:01-07:00","id":1443280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443273#post1443273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about all of the bat family!<br /> <br /> Including Cassandra Cain. I guess she\u2019s a assimite trained since birth</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes me wonder if<b> Dick Grayson </b>grew up among the <b>Midnight Circus</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Jason Todd </b>would have been put through the Initiation Rites by the Joker and is still trying to recover from it. Probably Low Humanity/Path of Night.<br /> <br /> <b>Tim Drake </b>might still be a ghoul or training for the Embrace or the newest of the Bat Family.<br /> <br /> <b>Barbara Gordon</b> would be someone who possibly was Embraced to repair the damage done to her. But is aloof from the family. You could do some interesting tragedy where she was initially a ghoul, crippled, and then Batman held off on Embracing her until recently. Possibly the Embrace didn't cure her and she has to use a Rouse check to cure it every night she wants to go out.<br /> <br /> Agreed on <b>Cassandra Cain </b>being Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> <b>Stephanie </b><b>Brown </b>would be someone I would make a very High Generation &quot;adopted&quot; Robin that was always meant to be a training tool for Tim Drake but became something else. Maybe make her a Brujah, Toreador, or Thin Blood.<br /> <br /> If we include <b>Helena Bertinelli</b>, I'd almost certainly make her a non-Necromantic <b>Giovanni</b>/<b>Hecata</b>.<br /> <br /> I had <b>Kathy Kane </b>not Embraced by Bruce but a different lineage of Tzimisce Family, highlighting what a twisted and messed up bloodline the Kanes and Waynes were. With her devoted to stopping her PMC-running father and Malkavian crazy sister.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T17:49:53-07:00","id":1443311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443236#post1443236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's been deeply fun and deeply stupid too.<br /> <br /> All very good suggestions!<br /> <br /> Some ideas I am now having:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Mr. Freeze</b> as a outside context problem would work very well if you wanted to make him into a Son of Ether with lots of Paradox that he's dealing with. Maybe even verging on Marauder-dom and just stepping out of sci-fi Pulp in the vampire's world. Maybe his delusion is his wife is still alive and not DEAD inside his crogenics chamber (mind you, that's not an issue for mages necessarily). It actually explains why Batman and company can survive their fights with Freeze because they can survive being frozen better than most poor bastards.</div> </div> </div> </div>He makes a Great Tragic Quiet and thus why you can't really just.. HELP HIM. You can't fix him. And it sucks.... but you may not be able able even kill him. He's something you spend countless resources covering up and hope you don't get a visit from the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> So about other fun bat characters....<br /> <br /> Task Force X/sucide Squad. The Second Inquisition gathers a bunch of monsters to do to hunt Monsters.. THIS CANNOT POSSIBLY GO WRONG. I would imagine this is where Harley becomes a Real vampire rather than ghoul because its where her story sort becomes herown. Also it lets you Throw a wereshark at players.<br /> <br /> Azrael-....is unchanged. He's a hunter with magical armor who kills the shti out of vampires... he actually is TAMER by making him in the WOD than DC.<br /> <br /> Sy- is a semi retired Technocrat.<br /> <br /> Bane-is a brujah trying to reclaim the whole &quot;clan of the learnend&quot; and he will break your back to prove it. He is very much a being that demonstrates someone who is deep on the path of Entelenchy<br /> <br /> Mad Hatter is... too easy but sometimes you want the Dominate malk who's going around playing mad hatter.<br /> <br /> Terry Macguiness- THe Mortalish Descendant of Bruce Wayne(I say mortalish because he could be a Revanant, a Dhampyr etc) That he is the living descendant in some fashion is.. I think useful plot to play off people.<br /> <br /> Kite-man is the little shovelhead that could. He's got luck/nine lives etc.. everyone knows he's a joke.. and yet he keeps coming back.<br /> <br /> OK! Really over the top idea... to cut down on the &quot;Everyone is a malkavian&quot; There is a Malkavian Elder named Arkam many of the one off villains..(calendar man, victor zaz..) are just his personalities going out and possessing someone. For extra fun he's a diablerist. For Extra Extra fun these just create new personalities.. that fight to escape and take over. The Jokers... being some of the more effective ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T17:55:15-07:00","id":1443312,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the Order of Saint Dumas is pretty much the Society of Leopold as is.<br /> <br /> Task Force X also works as a Technocracy idea post-Avatar Storm if we're going full WOD. &quot;The Technocracy is reduced to a fraction of its previous strength. What to do? I know, explosive implants and have other monsters hunt for you!&quot;<br /> <br /> Yes, what could possibly go wrong.<br /> <br /> Though Amanda Waller would fit into the SI or Technocracy just fine. Like Azrael she's a character that fits into the world very well.<br /> <br /> To dip into other Justice Leaguers:<br /> <br /> * Diana: Black Fury seems almost too obvious doesn't it? As a vampire, I'd probably make her a Ventrue. Though then I'd make her flat out a Methuselah waking up in the Modern World.<br /> <br /> * Deathstroke: Banu Haqim of the &quot;Embraced White Guy&quot; variety but still pretty Web of Knives. He kills other vampires and supernaturals for money. No need for him to be elsewise.<br /> <br /> * The Penguin: You know, he could also work well as one of the Giovanni's branch families. What sort of sick fucks were the Cobblepots? The Giovanni's sort of sick fucks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-09-2021, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T18:47:12-07:00","id":1443316,"title":"","content":"<i>Peyton Riley</i> (the second <b>Ventriloquist</b>) is a Daughter of Cacophony who uses ventriloquism rather than singing as the Performance focus for her Melpominee discipline. <br /> <br /> <b>The Eraser</b> (<i>Lenny Fiasco</i>) is the vampire you turn to when you need to cover up a potential Masquerade breach. He will go to the scene of the crime and erase any evidence that might potentially tie it to vampires - or even any sign that it ever happened in the first place, if feasible - and in exchange, you will own him a serious boon in the future. (And yes, he is a real Batman villain.) Clan is probably irrelevant, though in my head I kind of like Ravnos. (Tremere also works well.) <br /> <br /> <b>Orca</b> (<i>Dr. Grace Balin</i>) is a Gangrel Mariner, marine biologist, and environmental activist. (Because I actually liked Larry Hama's brief run on Batman.) <br /> <br /> <b>The Clock King</b> (the Batman: The Animated Series version) is an Assamite Vizier/Scholar with an obsession with time-keeping, planning, and minutia. Everything he does is planned down to the second and his ability to plan and predict events are second to none. <br /> <br /> <i>Warren White</i>, <b>The Great White Shark</b>, a former inside trader and crooked financier who was sent to prison for a long time. He was embraced by a vengeful Nosferatu angry at White losing (read, stealing) his money. Now, with pale white, hairless skin, no nose, lips or ears, and serrated teeth, he runs a mini criminal empire, financing other criminals' (and vampires') exploits in exchange for a cut, all from his jail cell. <br /> <br /> <b>Dragonfly</b>, <b>Silken Spider</b>, and <b>Tiger Moth</b> are <i>Public Enemies</i>, a punk rock trio well known to the city's underground clubs. No one knows their real names (though they sometimes refer to each other as Phyllis, Roxanne and Mary). Pick whichever Clans you want, though I think Ravnos, Setite and Toreador (in some order) would be interesting. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T19:07:13-07:00","id":1443323,"title":"","content":"Let me tackle another Mr. Freeze:<br /> <br /> <b>Victor Frieze</b> was a Tremere scientist who was attempting to experiment with technomancy and necromancy both to resurrect his dead wife. His sire, <b>Maximillian Strauss</b> for a Bloodlines connection, was furious at this dillution of Blood Sorcery as well a needless sentimentality for a past life. Destroying his laboratory and leaving him to burn in the fire, the magic involved as well as necromantic artifacts resulted in him becoming doubly cursed. Perhaps also because his fury awakened something in the blood the Tremere stole from Saulot or Tzimisce as well.<br /> <br /> The Freeze Bloodline, of which he is the only one, is possessed of a Disciplines of <b>Cryos</b>, <b>Blood Sorcery</b> (Technomancy), and <b>Fortitude</b> with his Old Disciplines being fairly weak. It also has the Discipline of being weakened in great heat and taking double damage from fire or sunlight.<br /> <br /> Freize is doubly cursed because while he continues to experiment on his wife's body, the Giovanni have already informed him that his quest is doomed. Nora Freize did not produce a Wraith when she died and has gone on to whatever true afterlife awaits mortals (or Oblivion). Instead, he seeks Biothaumatigical Experimentation or other secrets that could only produce a facimile of his wife or a body for something...else.<br /> <br /> If you want to tone down the crazy (why) he can be a blue skinned frozen man in a trench coat with the power of ice. If you want to play it up, he has created a Masquerade-breaching technomancy modified diving suit from the 1940s to counteract his curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T19:09:46-07:00","id":1443325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443316#post1443316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Peyton Riley</i> (the second <b>Ventriloquist</b>) is a Daughter of Cacophony who uses ventriloquism rather than singing as the Performance focus for her Melpominee discipline.<br /> <br /> <b>The Eraser</b> (<i>Lenny Fiasco</i>) is the vampire you turn to when you need to cover up a potential Masquerade breach. He will go to the scene of the crime and erase any evidence that might potentially tie it to vampires - or even any sign that it ever happened in the first place, if feasible - and in exchange, you will own him a serious boon in the future. (And yes, he is a real Batman villain.) Clan is probably irrelevant, though in my head I kind of like Ravnos. (Tremere also works well.)<br /> <br /> <b>Orca</b> (<i>Dr. Grace Balin</i>) is a Gangrel Mariner, marine biologist, and environmental activist. (Because I actually liked Larry Hama's brief run on Batman.)<br /> <br /> <b>The Clock King</b> (the Batman: The Animated Series version) is an Assamite Vizier/Scholar with an obsession with time-keeping, planning, and minutia. Everything he does is planned down to the second and his ability to plan and predict events are second to none.<br /> <br /> <i>Warren White</i>, <b>The Great White Shark</b>, a former inside trader and crooked financier who was sent to prison for a long time. He was embraced by a vengeful Nosferatu angry at White losing (read, stealing) his money. Now, with pale white, hairless skin, no nose, lips or ears, and serrated teeth, he runs a mini criminal empire, financing other criminals' (and vampires') exploits in exchange for a cut, all from his jail cell.<br /> <br /> <b>Dragonfly</b>, <b>Silken Spider</b>, and <b>Tiger Moth</b> are <i>Public Enemies</i>, a punk rock trio well known to the city's underground clubs. No one knows their real names (though they sometimes refer to each other as Phyllis, Roxanne and Mary). Pick whichever Clans you want, though I think Ravnos, Setite and Toreador (in some order) would be interesting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are great but I'm confused why you wouldn't make the Clock King the obvious choice: TRUE BRUJAH!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I mean, he's got the attitude and personality down pat plus he can seemingly kick Batman's ass despite the latter being so much more skilled combat wise.<br /> <br /> I also wonder if Warren White just is a Gangrel with frenzy problems.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T19:32:06-07:00","id":1443326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443325#post1443325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of these are great but I'm confused why you wouldn't make the Clock King the obvious choice: TRUE BRUJAH!</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, much like Rodents of Unusual Size, I don't believe they exist. <br /> <br /> More seriously, I just enjoy the idea of Assamites who completely avoid any of the usual &quot;middle eastern assassin&quot; tropes. <br /> <br /> <b> Magpie </b>(<i>Margaret Pye</i>) is both a master thief and a skilled forger who usually leaves behind fakes of the &quot;shinies&quot; she collects (steals). She's a Toreador, probably originally from Britain. <br /> <br /> Another Toreador is <i>Louis Guinnessey</i>, originally from Quebec. He is the archetypical gentleman criminal and thief, akin to Arsene Lupin and Sir Charles Litton, who prefers to steal from the wealthy for his own amusement and financial advancement. He makes it a point of pride that his thefts and heists never involve any violence. He has a particular fascination with scent, especially perfumes and flowers, particularly his trademark lilacs. This, combined with his penchant for lavender hued clothing, has earned him the nickname <b>Louis the Lilac</b> (which sounds like &quot;Louie&quot; because of the French pronunciation). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T19:39:13-07:00","id":1443328,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Catwoman, rather than Gangrel or Toreador, would make an interesting Ministry member.<br /> <br /> Maybe with a &quot;touched by Bast&quot; sort of religious angle but seductive, corruptive, and thieving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T19:51:41-07:00","id":1443329,"title":"","content":"She could always be a Lasombra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-09T23:36:36-07:00","id":1443337,"title":"","content":"One of my Weird Ideas which I'm unlikely to ever implement in an actual chronicle would be to introduce &quot;Batman&quot; (more likely some similarly inspired vigilante) as an aberrant force (no relation to the eponymous splat) in the setting. He'd be a &quot;normal&quot; human albeit one with peak physical stats and high-tech gear. A challenging foe for a Neonate perhaps, but no match for Vampiric Disciplines. The real interesting question (for me) would be in the reaction of Kindred society to this strange occurrence. A human with billions of dollars in resources waging a one-man crusade on crime..... if left unchecked, he will inevitably begin to interfere with the Kindreds' clandestine operations, which frequently utilize the mortal underworld. Do the PCs elliminate him? Do they attempt to subvert or make use of this singular mortal? As the heir to a vast fortune and business empire, does he unwittingly have any attachments to Kindred assets already? What happens when intrigued Kindred begin competing to influence this odd mortal? Could he end up ghouled or even embraced? A somewhat silly idea, but one which could make for an interesting scenario maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","user":"Ventrue Busboy","date":". 04-10-2021, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26710-ventrue-busboy","name":"Ventrue Busboy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26710_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T09:43:14-07:00","id":1443372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443280#post1443280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes me wonder if<b> Dick Grayson </b>grew up among the <b>Midnight Circus</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Jason Todd </b>would have been put through the Initiation Rites by the Joker and is still trying to recover from it. Probably Low Humanity/Path of Night.<br /> <br /> <b>Tim Drake </b>might still be a ghoul or training for the Embrace or the newest of the Bat Family.<br /> <br /> <b>Barbara Gordon</b> would be someone who possibly was Embraced to repair the damage done to her. But is aloof from the family. You could do some interesting tragedy where she was initially a ghoul, crippled, and then Batman held off on Embracing her until recently. Possibly the Embrace didn't cure her and she has to use a Rouse check to cure it every night she wants to go out.<br /> <br /> Agreed on <b>Cassandra Cain </b>being Banu Haqim.<br /> <br /> <b>Stephanie </b><b>Brown </b>would be someone I would make a very High Generation &amp;quot;adopted&amp;quot; Robin that was always meant to be a training tool for Tim Drake but became something else. Maybe make her a Brujah, Toreador, or Thin Blood.<br /> <br /> If we include <b>Helena Bertinelli</b>, I'd almost certainly make her a non-Necromantic <b>Giovanni</b>/<b>Hecata</b>.<br /> <br /> I had <b>Kathy Kane </b>not Embraced by Bruce but a different lineage of Tzimisce Family, highlighting what a twisted and messed up bloodline the Kanes and Waynes were. With her devoted to stopping her PMC-running father and Malkavian crazy sister.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Cassandra Cain like character that was trained from such a young age. But when set on her first mission realized she hates killing and ran away, is a pretty facasnating character, also the fact she can\u2019t talk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T20:36:27-07:00","id":1443439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443312#post1443312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * Diana: Black Fury seems almost too obvious doesn't it? As a vampire, I'd probably make her a Ventrue. Though then I'd make her flat out a Methuselah waking up in the Modern World.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>She's a strong, she's fast. Not so tough.. but inspires people. IF She's not a Sister of Hippolita. She's a Brujah and she's Old. Honestly make her a female Critas.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443328#post1443328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Catwoman, rather than Gangrel or Toreador, would make an interesting Ministry member.<br /> <br /> Maybe with a &quot;touched by Bast&quot; sort of religious angle but seductive, corruptive, and thieving.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ministry is a good choice especially since its not longer &quot;SNAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKES'<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So more ideas for why Gotham is.. Special. You can't really kill anyone. There is something about the Archtypes in the city that just keep coming back. Maybe you can kill the Prince but they will always be a batman. This is especially true about Diablere You eat the person they tend to wear you a suit. Everyone knows this.. its just part of Gotham. But even if you kill the Penguin.... another one just eventually shows up... and they seem to know stuff maybe they aren't the exact person but they are near enough.. maybe one was a Nos and now there's a Giovanni but.. he remembers stuff he shouldn't.. he's acting in ways he shouldn't...<br /> <br /> Like Solmon Grundy there's just.. something wrong with the city. Something scary wrong and yet...vampires know the power is theirs to take. Even in the World of Darkness Gotham should be fucked up. It probably should be Midwest bad for getting in and out... well getting out anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T02:56:38-07:00","id":1443455,"title":"","content":"The Followers of set always had front cults that weren't &quot;SNAAAAAAAAAKES&quot; <br /> <br /> Some thoughts; <br /> The City gives free reign for batman to go around causing trouble in other people's domains, because he doesn't kill anyone, and because the damage he does actually works to the advantage of the local kindred population: Prices might go down, Insurance goes up, certain businesses and market prices are effected, windows are broken and so many other conditions occur; The vamp playing &quot;Gordon&quot; knows these things and actually facilitates batman raids with the criminals, or the sponsors of these criminals, that batman is going to fight. Everyone who knows what they're doing can capitalize on these events. <br /> <br /> Some Villains are just going to be proxies of a vampire who can't be bothered to act out the conflict himself. <br /> <br /> Some Villains are going to have multiple Actors because accidents happen and Malkavians are Malkavians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T03:04:21-07:00","id":1443456,"title":"","content":"Batman beating up people left and right every night is no different from any other Kindred feeding. Heck, all vampires do harm mortals every night as a nature of their existence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If Batman were a Ventrue, he might also have the feeding restriction of criminals.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Arkham was also his Herd and he needed the power of his fellow Kindred to keep him going toward the end of his career.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-11-2021, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T08:09:24-07:00","id":1443470,"title":"","content":"Most of my exposure to Gotham City is from the <i>Gotham </i>series. I also saw that film in which Uma Thurman plays Ivy.<br /> <br /> The Court of Owls are a coterie of the city's elders and mostly Ventrue. They survive and prosper by nurturing a chaotic and flamboyant environment that directs attention away from them and deters outsiders, although such a passive strategy can leave them unprepared for direct conflict.<br /> <br /> Hugo Strange is the Tremere regent, loyal to whomever will patronise his research and not kill him.<br /> <br /> Theodore Galavan was a Tzimisce revenant with connections to the colonial Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Barbara Kean is the childe of Jason Skolimski, a Toreador serial killer who admired her and believed that she'd flourish after the embrace.<br /> <br /> Ivy's an indepedent blood sorcerer, either Tremere or a kind of failed Bahari convert.<br /> <br /> Penguin discovered vampires on his own initiative, having worked for them by several degrees of separation. He forced the first one he found and could coerce to embrace him, so he's Caitiff.<br /> <br /> Victor Zsasz is an older neonate who prefers to spend most of his time with kine and has no interest kindred affairs beyond his job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T08:15:47-07:00","id":1443471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave#post1443157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I freely admit to currently running Gotham City by Night where Batman was the Old Clan Tzimisce Prince and opposed by the Malkavian Antitribu Joker.<br /> <br /> The PCs' territory is Bludhaven, which I'm basically doing as Gary meets Detroit exaggerated to comic book levels.<br /> <br /> I'm having a lot of fun with the sheer silliness of playing &amp;quot;The DC Universe except everyone is a vampire&amp;quot; weirdness.<br /> <br /> Vandal Savage is the head of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any ideas how they'd adapt things from the DCU (or Hell, Marvel) to V:TM?</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds really cool but idk enough about the DCU to really comment. Could some of the villains be other supernaturals (maybe Poison Ivy as a radical Verbena)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T08:18:28-07:00","id":1443472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443471#post1443471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds really cool but idk enough about the DCU to really comment. Could some of the villains be other supernaturals (maybe Poison Ivy as a radical Verbena)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Very probably.<br /> <br /> I'm mostly just spitballing here for the fun of it. I figured everyone else would enjoy a chance to do a less than serious take on the World of Darkness. While I tended to do a Vampire-based one, you could easily make Bruce Wayne a Son of Ether or Hunter or something else in a World of Darkness city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1443470#post1443470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of my exposure to Gotham City is from the <i>Gotham </i>series. I also saw that film in which Uma Thurman plays Ivy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotham was quite fun and one of the rare things that focused on the city itself in terms of it being a comic book hellhole of a city (and so much fun).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Court of Owls are a coterie of the city's elders and mostly Ventrue. They survive and prosper by nurturing a chaotic and flamboyant environment that directs attention away from them and deters outsiders, although such a passive strategy can leave them unprepared for direct conflict. </div> </div> </div>I always feel it was a missed opportunity not to call it the Parliament of Owls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[]