y only suggesting (low levels of it) it for agile types like Bat-Fam and Catwoman and the obvious strength types. The Joker wouldn't have Potence, Nor two-face or scarecrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T10:04:57-07:00","id":1444349,"title":"","content":"I'm largely giving obfuscate to characters to keep this 'world of crimefighting' secret from the masses. Some other disciplines are just there to emulate somewhat less realistic gadgets, like batman's ability to glide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T10:07:02-07:00","id":1444350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1444349#post1444349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm largely giving obfuscate to characters to keep this 'world of crimefighting' secret from the masses. Some other disciplines are just there to emulate somewhat less realistic gadgets, like batman's ability to glide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, people may have heard of the Legend of the Batman but do they believe he's a VAMPIRE?<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is probably utterly steeped in inaccurate urban legends. The internet probably looks....actually the internet is probably the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T18:04:49-07:00","id":1444416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1444346#post1444346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, while parkor is impressive, the canonical Catwoman DOESN'T have superpowers. So clearly most of what she has is just Athletics and Dexterity anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except when she's an immortal being or at least one with 9 lives thanks to the magic of cats. Batman is a weird mix of stories over the years after all.<br /> <br /> Honestly I don't think &quot;batman would need physicals at 2 to function&quot; is a way to get a defining set of clan/bloodline disciplines for the character, at best they are required for everyone to play and thus are bought out of clan(or you redo the game with physicals as Universal with Each clan having 3 mentals/socials). There are very few characters I think of in Batman who are defined by their inhuman level of resillience, strength or Speed even if that would probably be required to be Batman.<br /> <br /> Bane is clearly on another level than batman for physical strength. This is why I would say its an inclan for him<br /> <br /> Clayface- He seems to be superhumanly strong in a toss around cars level.<br /> <br /> Killer croc-ugly and super strong it makes his clan pretty obvious.<br /> <br /> Mr Freize-He seems to show a low level of it.. but it my be inhuman stamina...<br /> <br /> But is batman? I mean having a couple points at low level probably helps you run around as batman but I would not say its a defining feature for him.<br /> <br /> Celerity is.. harder. Batman doesn't have any speedster enemies though if we look at characters who show superior dexterity. Most of them are Like Lady Shiva or Bronze Tiger, or Richard Dragon it comes from superior martial art training, But debateably ones who might have it as an INCLAN <br /> <br /> Bane: because he is better than you in all ways.<br /> <br /> Dick Grayson-He's definately the superior acrobat to Batman this could just represent greater purchase out of clan, a hold over from ghouling etc.<br /> <br /> Catwoman-she is better than batman in this regard at the least and superhuman grace might be a definable point for her, but this sort of pulls her back into being a Toreador. Her theft is driven by her need for beauty, Auspex gives her plenty of cat tricks to wrap things up and she only would need a token buy into Animalism.<br /> <br /> Harley Quinn-Honestly she's a moving Target but like Dick she shows off a lot carnival dex tricks and unlike him she wasn't raised as a part of it.<br /> <br /> Fortitude is not as hard as celerity but generally its sort of part of the package that comes with super strength there aren't so many I would think of who are hard to hurt who aren't tossing around cars. This generally where Bane and Killer croc sits. Bane of course having weaknesses of his Venom set<br /> <br /> Clayface-he does have the superstrength option but he's you know also made out of clay so he's pretty solid on both..<br /> <br /> Mr. Freize-He's a rare example of the other direction he comes off as relatively resiliant(aside from his heat weakness) who may require certain levels of strength to be effective.<br /> <br /> <br /> With this in mind.. I'm going to lay out what i think are the defining powers of batman. I Do Think he is a serious buyer out of clan but they are clearly something he hasn't maxed with various types clearly out doing him.<br /> <br /> So what does he generally demonstrate, Stealth and disguise-Well that's obfuscate. Does he demonstrate any real animal control? Rarely. and he's not super humanly strong or deformed.<br /> <br /> Presence would help with his Bruce Wayne identity. And having the more opened up VV version of protean So he wouldn't be a BAD member of hte Ministry... but meh<br /> <br /> Dominate would also help alot with the whole establishing an identity and alibis(&quot;Of course I remember seeing bruce there..&quot;) Auspex is a really good detective power....Batman as a malkavian is a bit too easy though.<br /> <br /> There's probably some version of Tzim that gets you Auspex, Dominate and Protean.. that gives you a bunch of neat tricks. and a wonderfully unique wayne bloodline.<br /> <br /> <br /> It might just be easier to build bloodlines for various villains and heroes coming out of various clans rather than have them match up perfectly then it gives the players some buy in? I Yeah sure we are talking about catwoman as an npc lover to an npc prince... but that's not as interesting as making her your sire or broodmate or mentor or enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T18:12:10-07:00","id":1444418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's probably some version of Tzim that gets you Auspex, Dominate and Protean.. that gives you a bunch of neat tricks. and a wonderfully unique wayne bloodline. </div> </div> </div>He's Fifth Edition Tzimisce!<br /> <br /> RUN!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It might just be easier to build bloodlines for various villains and heroes coming out of various clans rather than have them match up perfectly then it gives the players some buy in? I Yeah sure we are talking about catwoman as an npc lover to an npc prince... but that's not as interesting as making her your sire or broodmate or mentor or enemy. </div> </div> </div>Yes, as much as I love Batman, an interesting Chronicle pretty much has to be either him taken out of the picture.<br /> <br /> * Torpor<br /> * Final Death<br /> * Beckoned<br /> * Leaving the city to go fight in the Gehenna War<br /> <br /> And it'd be a good idea for Selina to have broken up with Bruce too. Probably because he's just too...Princey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T21:28:53-07:00","id":1444439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1444418#post1444418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's Fifth Edition Tzimisce!<br /> <br /> RUN!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, as much as I love Batman, an interesting Chronicle pretty much has to be either him taken out of the picture.<br /> <br /> * Torpor<br /> * Final Death<br /> * Beckoned<br /> * Leaving the city to go fight in the Gehenna War<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Him being the active prince isn't a bad choice being a part of the court and trying to work your way into the bat Family while dealing with is an option... or something to Fight. This isn't DC comics where batman always wins. He can easily be the camarilla prince that is the Man who keeps things down. Really he's no different than Critias or any other npc with a decent amount of power. Nothing about him has screamed for example &quot;batman needs to be a fourth gen vampire he could easily be a standard new world prince.. 8th gen.. with a decent spread of discplines but nothing super crazy Auspex 5, Protean 5, Dominate 5. Out of clan obfuscate.. some basic physicals.. bam batman.<br /> <br /> Hell that didn't even require any blood magic he's practically tame for a Camarilla Prince(though having acess to blood magical items does cover the whole gadget thing)<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly my go to for this campain would be something like the Harley Quinn series. The New Powers on the block can and do kill the old. So I say again.. Batman works as A mentor, the prince you need to play with.. or the guy you are going to kill. Taking him off screen removes alot of the fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 04-18-2021, 12:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T11:08:40-07:00","id":1444523,"title":"","content":"The thing with Batman is that in most incarnations his attributes are something stupid like... 5/5/5, 5/5/5, 5/5/5. I heard he uses a version of Venom (bane's wonder-steroid) which makes that somewhat more possible but you simply can't be nine fives without getting magic or hypertech involved. Honestly I find the idea of an all-natural batman less realistic than the comedian from the 5th dimension that sometimes deigns to plague superman. Furthermore a number of Batman's signature gadgets aren't feasible with todays tech; the grappling hook gun and the gliding cape being big offenders, but also I don't think you could really do batterangs either. (also a lot of Batman's enemies make extensive use of knockout gas, which isn't a thing afaik) <br /> <br /> Giving out lots of low level disciplines, or getting generous with mage $enhancements is really the way to make more reasonable characters. Especially because at 5/5/5 physicals... that really isn't enough for a few hours of high intensity activity while carrying a belt full of heavy tools while also accounting for all the injuries you're going to pile up. You've also got the issue of Batman being tall and built like a body builder, which might be great in a brawl, but acrobatic feats aren't kind on big and heavy dudes; there's a reason why olympic gymnasts are tiny, it gives them an advantage. On the otherhand with younger robins... high-skill, relatively small size; without relying on a dangerous weapon, a semi-competent man just needs to engage in a grapple to win. Both have a need for Potence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T15:54:29-07:00","id":1444560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443157-gotham-city-by-night-a-k-a-to-the-bat-cave?p=1444523#post1444523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Batman is that in most incarnations his attributes are something stupid like... 5/5/5, 5/5/5, 5/5/5. I heard he uses a version of Venom (bane's wonder-steroid) which makes that somewhat more possible but you simply can't be nine fives without getting magic or hypertech involved. Honestly I find the idea of an all-natural batman less realistic than the comedian from the 5th dimension that sometimes deigns to plague superman. Furthermore a number of Batman's signature gadgets aren't feasible with todays tech; the grappling hook gun and the gliding cape being big offenders, but also I don't think you could really do batterangs either. (also a lot of Batman's enemies make extensive use of knockout gas, which isn't a thing afaik)<br /> <br /> Giving out lots of low level disciplines, or getting generous with mage $enhancements is really the way to make more reasonable characters. Especially because at 5/5/5 physicals... that really isn't enough for a few hours of high intensity activity while carrying a belt full of heavy tools while also accounting for all the injuries you're going to pile up. You've also got the issue of Batman being tall and built like a body builder, which might be great in a brawl, but acrobatic feats aren't kind on big and heavy dudes; there's a reason why olympic gymnasts are tiny, it gives them an advantage. On the otherhand with younger robins... high-skill, relatively small size; without relying on a dangerous weapon, a semi-competent man just needs to engage in a grapple to win. Both have a need for Potence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Batman is an unrealistic character. Batman is perhaps the most super powered character in Dc comics. But if I wanted a Realistic game I wouldn't be running &quot;Batman is a vampire&quot; and I sure as hell wouldn't be using any of V:TM for something realistic. But if getting to a Batman who works for my chronicle requires half a dozen disciplines and maxed traits it doesn't matter? Batman's &quot;clan&quot; is clearly not Super strong or or tough even if you'd need them to be batman.. they are just.. genre conceits.<br /> <br /> He might be celerity defined with how much acrobatics and grace is built in... but He's no Bane.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T16:10:06-07:00","id":1444562,"title":"","content":"Besides, vampires can raise their stats temporarily. I do think Batman at a 100 years may have pretty high Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&